---
/**
 * Hero — the homepage's, in the site's shared background form (2026-10-02)
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The spec §7 copy — eyebrow, three-stanza H1, description, CTA, secondary
 * link — laid over a FULL-BLEED photograph instead of beside one. The
 * structure is the shared `BackgroundHero` (promoted to the core the day the
 * homepage adopted the shape); what lives here is only what is the
 * homepage's own:
 *
   *   · the three stanzas and their line breaks, passed as a `title` slot
   *     because the H1 is structure, not a string (spec §7 forbids collapsing
   *     them; read end to end they produce the spec §26 sentence). Each
   *     stanza's lines are spans that stack on small screens and join onto one
   *     line at desktop width (see home.css);
   *   · the `.bg-hero--home` modifier, whose rules in home.css set the display
   *     face and the H1 size (48px cap since 2026-10-02) and space the stanzas
   *     (band height now lives in the core `.bg-hero__inner`, shared by every
   *     background hero since 2026-10-02);
   *
   * CHANGED FORM, SAME COMPLIANCE NOTE — the spec draws this section as a
   * split ("Left: 5 columns / Right: 7 columns") while also mandating a 64–72px
   * hero and five exact lines; those were already irreconcilable (the old
   * split-column build measured it: the widest mandated line is 594px at 64px,
   * wider than any 5-column block in this grid). The stanza separation won then
   * and it wins now. With the photograph moved behind the copy there is no
   * column split left to honour. The 64–72px range was set aside on 2026-10-02
   * (48px cap) to shorten the band, and the five hard <br> breaks became spans
   * that only stack on small screens — desktop joins each stanza onto one line.
   * Both are deliberate, owner-requested deviations from §7.
 *
 * The image caption went with the old frame: a photograph behind the copy has
 * no figure to caption, and the slot's `alt` is empty for the same reason —
 * see `BackgroundHero.astro` and the `heroSourcing` note in `media.js`.
 */
import BackgroundHero from './BackgroundHero.astro';
import { hero } from '../data/home.js';
---

<BackgroundHero
  eyebrow={hero.eyebrow}
  description={hero.description}
  primaryCta={hero.primaryCta}
  secondaryCta={hero.secondaryCta}
  imageKey={hero.image.key}
  class="bg-hero--home"
  titleId="hero-title"
>
  <Fragment slot="title">
    {
      hero.stanzas.map((stanza) => (
        <span class="bg-hero__stanza">
          {stanza.lines.map((line) => (
            <span class="bg-hero__line">{line}</span>
          ))}
        </span>
      ))
    }
  </Fragment>
</BackgroundHero>
